1
00:04:10,909 --> 00:04:16,909
In this house... if you've seen one ghost... you haven't seen them all.

2
00:08:21,818 --> 00:08:27,818
Beetlejuice is a fantasy, comedy film directed by Tim Burton.

3
00:12:32,727 --> 00:12:38,727
A newly dead New England couple seeks help from a deranged demon exorcist
to scare an affluent New York family out of their home.

4
00:16:43,636 --> 00:16:49,636
Adam, played by Alec Baldwin.

5
00:20:54,545 --> 00:21:00,545
Barbara, played by Geena Davis.

6
00:25:05,454 --> 00:25:11,454
Lydia, played by Winona Ryder.

7
00:29:16,363 --> 00:29:22,363
Delia, played by Catherine O'Hara.

8
00:33:27,272 --> 00:33:33,272
Charles, played by Jeffrey Jones.

9
00:37:38,181 --> 00:37:44,181
Betelgeuse, played by Michael Keaton.

10
00:41:49,090 --> 00:41:55,090
Beetlejuice is a 1988 American gothic horror comedy film directed by Tim Burton from a screenplay by
Michael McDowell and Warren Skaaren based on a story by McDowell and Larry Wilson.

11
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
The film stars Michael Keaton as Betelgeuse, along with Alec Baldwin, Geena
Davis, Jeffrey Jones, Catherine O'Hara and Winona Ryder.

12
00:50:10,909 --> 00:50:16,909
The plot revolves around Adam and Barbara Maitland, a recently deceased couple.

13
00:54:21,818 --> 00:54:27,818
As ghosts, they are not allowed to leave their house.

14
00:58:32,727 --> 00:58:38,727
They contact Betelgeuse, a sleazy "bio-exorcist", to
scare the house's new inhabitants away.

15
01:02:43,636 --> 01:02:49,636
The film prominently features music from Harry
Belafonte's albums Calypso and Jump Up Calypso.

16
01:06:54,545 --> 01:07:00,545
Beetlejuice was released in the United States on March 30, 1988, by Warner Bros.

17
01:11:05,454 --> 01:11:11,454
The film was a critical and commercial success, grossing
$84 million against a $15 million budget.

18
01:15:16,363 --> 01:15:22,363
It won the Academy Award for Best Makeup and three Saturn Awards: Best Horror
Film, Best Makeup, and Best Supporting Actress for Sylvia Sidney.

19
01:19:27,272 --> 01:19:33,272
The film's success spawned a media franchise, consisting of an animated television series,
video games, a 2018 stage musical, and a 2024 sequel, Beetlejuice Beetlejuice.

20
01:23:38,181 --> 01:23:44,181
The film explores themes of skeleton, afterlife, calypso, supernatural, arts.

21
01:27:49,090 --> 01:27:55,090
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending.
